And here I am posting from my old, old home machine with a 1 G disk and
32 M RAM, running X, XEmacs, Netscape, and occasionally NetHack (with
color tiles).  Admittedly its Linux installation is also a bit antique
and lovingly hand-hacked to keep memory usage down.  If you install a
modern Linux distribution whose X interface is likely to depend on some
bloated psychedelic nightmare like KDE or GNOME, then you will need more
ridiculous amounts of memory.

Also, X11 NetHack does not _default_ to using tiles; you have to set the
"NetHack.tile_file" resource to enable them.

